1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,330
How many folds would it take
to reach the Moon?

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:08,190
How many folds to reach the Moon?

3
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,160
Let's start folding

4
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:13,680
Every fold doubles the thickness!

5
00:00:13,730 --> 00:00:16,650
5 folds: only 3.2 mm…
still thin

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:19,720
What if we keep going?

7
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:22,790
14 folds: as tall as a grown-up

8
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:25,860
27 folds: taller than Mount Everest

9
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:29,430
The answer is A! 42 folds
reach the Moon (about 384,000 km)

10
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,300
Each fold multiplies by 2

11
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:34,870
Doubling 42 times = about 4.4 trillion times

12
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:37,340
But real paper usually stops folding
at about 7 or 8 times

13
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:39,890
Try it yourself!
Tell us how many folds you got!

14
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:43,390
Which of the three
did you try?
